    "findings": [
      {
        "id": "QR-18.1-03",
        "severity": "HIGH",
        "category": "lifecycle and truthful interruption",
        "artifact": "src/dotnet/Vulgata.Infrastructure/Source/PreparedSourceReadContext.cs",
        "location": "ListAsync lines 75–120 and 262–265; SearchTextAsync lines 507–540; ReadTextRangeAsync lines 291–306; DisposeAsync lines 939–950",
        "affected_requirement": "spec.md FR-008; plan.md ID-A01 and ID-F02; contracts/prepared-source-tools.md lines 35, 51 and 103",
        "evidence": "ListAsync and SearchTextAsync check disposal in CheckAuthorityAsync before awaiting _listGate, but their semaphore waits use only caller cancellation and they do not recheck the disposed state after acquiring the gate. A call queued behind an active list/search can therefore pass its first check, wait while DisposeAsync cancels activity and closes _rootHandle, then resume against the closed handle and return Incomplete or ChangedInput instead of the distinct Cancelled outcome. ReadTextRangeAsync likewise has a window after its initial check and before OpenRelativeFile where disposal can turn a stopped call into a source failure. Existing disposal tests cover an active read awaiting final authority, not a queued operation or this open window.",
        "correction_outcome": "Add a public-seam controlled regression that disposes a context while a second operation is queued or between approval and open. Make queued/opening operations observe the context disposal token and return sanitized Cancelled while settling; keep the existing no-disclosure and owned-handle guarantees.",
        "earliest_owner": "implement"
      }
    ],
    "summary": "REVISE. QR-18.1-01 and QR-18.1-02 are resolved: nested listing now opens the requested directory through held-root no-follow traversal and reports immediate Repository-relative children; range reads compare observed file identity and metadata before and after reading and before disclosure. The two focused regressions, surrounding tests, and 117/117 prepared-source suite pass on the qualified Windows account. A separate disposal race remains in operations already past their first authority check. The scoped lesson and refreshed lookback match the correction. The 63 PostgreSQL-backed retained-source tests remain blocked by the absent administrator prerequisite; controlled tests do not establish immutable snapshots or real Worker/model/provider integration."
  }
